  "abstract": "Sheng ming wu xian wu jiang (生命無限無疆) is a short early Chinese-language Christian narrative by Karl Friedrich August Gützlaff (郭實獵, 1803–1851), printed in Singapore in 1838 (Daoguang 18) by the Jianxia Shuyuan (堅夏書院). It opens with the words \"in Guangzhou Prefecture there was a household\" and introduces Li Ling, who grew rich through trade and loves feasting and entertainment. It contrasts him with his poor neighbor Liu Dai and notes that after Li Ling falls ill, his drinking companions do not come to ask after him. Its closing columns use phrases such as \"new heaven and earth,\" \"how may everlasting life be obtained,\" and \"believing in Jesus\" to link eternal life with faith in Jesus. The dialogue closes with the group voicing its fear of death and asking why they should not willingly submit to the Savior.\n\nThe catalogue identifies Karl Friedrich August Gützlaff (郭實獵) as the author of the historical work. This dataset uses 14 fixed images, including 10 pages with main text, from Harvard-Yenching Library DRS 428712522. The AI-reviewed JSON, TXT and TEI transcription retains 115 unresolved comparison items. Full human collation is outstanding.",
